# Internal Record Links — Names Are Never Dead Text

Whenever the UI displays the name/title of another record, render it as a link
to that record. Example: an invoice shows its company name → clicking it opens
that company. Never show a related record's name as plain text when its id is
available; if the id isn't fetched, add it to the query.

## Route map

| Record | URL |
|---|---|
| Company | `/companies/{companyId}` |
| Contact | `/contacts/{contactId}` |
| Deal | `/deals/{dealId}` |
| Project | `/projects/{projectId}` |
| Task | `/projects/{projectId}/tasks/{taskId}` |
| Invoice | `/invoices/{invoiceId}` |
| DM / thread | `/messages/{threadId}` |

## Pattern

```tsx
import Link from "next/link";

// ✅ GOOD — name links to the record
{deal.company && (
  <Link
    href={`/companies/${deal.company.id}`}
    className="text-primary hover:underline"
  >
    {deal.company.name}
  </Link>
)}

// ❌ BAD — dead text, user has to go search for the company
<span>{deal.company?.name}</span>
```

## Rules

- Use next/link (`Link`), never `<a>` or `router.push` in an onClick span.
- Style: `text-primary hover:underline` so links are recognizable; keep the
  surrounding text size (`text-sm`, `text-body`, …).
- Inside a clickable row/card (tables, list rows, kanban cards), stop the
  parent handler: `onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}` on the Link.
- Links must keep an adequate tap target in touch contexts — don't shrink
  below the row's existing line height; add `py-1 -my-1` padding if needed.
- Composite labels ("Deal title · Company name") link each part to its own
  record, not the whole string to one of them.
- Don't link a record to itself (e.g. the company name in the header of that
  company's own detail page).
